    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0218" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 37 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Truman to Prime Minister Churchill
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d37-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d37-f2"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-05-28">28 May 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>
                    Stalin has informed me through Mr.
                        Hopkins that he would like to have
                    our three party meeting in the Berlin area and I will reply that I have no
                    objection to the Berlin area.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d37-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d37-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy
                    channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d37-f2" n="2" xml:id="d37-f2-content">
                <p>For the first two paragraphs of this message, omitted here, see <ref
                        target="#d142">document No. 142</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
